/ A list saved to .jsonl and read back is the same list, one element per line.
Start
- set %rows% = [{"a": 1}, {"a": 2}, "three"]
- save %rows% to 'roundtrip.jsonl'
- read file 'roundtrip.jsonl', write to %back%
- delete file 'roundtrip.jsonl'
- assert %back.count% equals 3
- assert %back% equals %rows%
